The 15 years Yuki's spent on this
planet have been one long battle.

34
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,120
The HIV is only part of it.

35
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:15,717
She's also been fighting the harsh reality
of her situation while in treatment.

36
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,957
There's no doubt the
clinical trials with the

37
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:21,158
Medicuboid caused her an
unimaginable amount of pain.

38
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:24,920
And still, somehow Yuki keeps hanging on.

39
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:28,960
Well, anyway, we should
let her get some rest now.

40
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,417
Come on, Yuki.

41
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:33,900
You can't lose.

42
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:36,340
I mean, you're second.

43
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:39,660
The ultimate Swordsman.

44
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:55,560
Take her hand. It's okay.

45
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:57,194
That's what she wants.

46
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:06,260
Doctor, can she use the Medicuboid now?

47
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:10,357
But, well, wouldn't she want
to spend her last moments here?

48
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:11,270
No.

49
00:05:11,353 --> 00:05:13,120
She wants to go back one last time.

50
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:16,800
Please, Doctor, let her
use the Medicuboid again.

51
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:25,517
It's going to take about
a minute to boot up.

52
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,430
Then what?

53
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:29,521
I'm going next door to
log in with the Amusphere.

54
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:32,119
Wait for me, Yuki.

55
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:33,070
I'm coming.

56
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:57,540
Thanks, Asuna.

57
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:01,957
I'm glad I got to see you again,
because I got something for you.

58
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:05,320
I can't believe I almost
forgot about it. Really?

59
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:07,601
What is it you wanted to give me?

60
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:10,200
Oh, um, I still gotta make it.

61
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:11,380
Hang on a sec.

62
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:34,337
I can't

63
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:41,420
believe

64
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:50,190
it.

65
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:52,130
Yuki!

66
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,100
That's weird.

67
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:04,560
I feel so weak all of a sudden.

68
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:07,560
I'm not in any pain or anything, though.

69
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:08,970
It's okay.

70
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:11,080
You're just a little tired is all.

71
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:13,264
You'll feel better if you rest.

72
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:15,320
Yeah, maybe.

73
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:17,780
Listen, Asuna.

74
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,560
Take this.

75
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:21,780
It's my original sword skill.

76
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:24,020
No, Yuki, I couldn't.

77
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:25,360
Oh, come on.

78
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:26,940
I want you to have it.

79
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:29,000
Open the window.

80
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,300
I gave it a cool name.

81
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,540
Mother's Rosario.

82
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:47,100
It'll keep you safe.

83
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:49,000
When you need it.

84
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:53,280
Thank you, Yuki.

85
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:54,840
I promise.

86
00:07:55,340 --> 00:07:57,060
I'll take good care of it.

87
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:59,580
And someday, when I leave this world,

88
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:03,559
I'll make sure to pass it
on to someone before I go.

89
00:08:04,020 --> 00:08:07,220
Your sword will live on
until the end of time.

90
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,400
Thank you.

91
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:21,757
Oh guys, come on.

92
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:23,620
We talked about this.

93
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:25,260
You promised.

94
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:26,700
No goodbyes.

95
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:28,474
Nah, you got it wrong.

96
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,384
We're all here to cheer you up.

97
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:34,617
When you get to the other
side, wait for us, okay?

98
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:36,582
We won't take too long, promise.

99
00:08:37,940 --> 00:08:39,637
What are you talking about?

100
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:43,060
If you get there too soon, I'll be pissed.

101
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,100
You know the deal.

102
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:46,937
You're hopeless without us.

103
00:08:47,020 --> 00:08:48,608
So don't even try to argue.

104
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,372
Just sit tight and wait.

105
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:52,330
For...

106
00:08:52,413 --> 00:08:53,243
for us.

107
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:55,200
Please, Nori, don't cry.

108
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,680
We promised we'd be strong.

109
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,657
I give up.

110
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:08,580
You win.

111
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,037
I'll wait for you.

112
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:13,480
But take your time.

113
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:14,840
You got it?

114
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:03,340
Look at all those fairies.

115
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:05,820
I'm sorry.

116
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,537
I had to let them know.

117
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:08,917
I hope you're not mad at me.

118
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,620
Are you kidding?

119
00:10:11,020 --> 00:10:12,700
Why would I be mad?

120
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,720
There's so many of them.

121
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:18,320
It's like a dream.

122
00:10:19,260 --> 00:10:20,860
Why are they here?

123
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,300
Because of you.

124
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:28,980
You're the strongest, most powerful
Swordsman this world's ever seen.

125
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:32,105
There will never be anyone
else like you again.

126
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:34,900
We can't let you go
without saying goodbye.

127
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:36,530
It's not right.

128
00:10:36,613 --> 00:10:39,220
We're all praying for you.

129
00:10:39,660 --> 00:10:44,860
That your next journey will be
to a place as wonderful as this.

130
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:48,580
I'm happy.

131
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:50,700
I'm so happy.

132
00:10:57,360 --> 00:11:00,477
You know this whole time I thought

133
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:04,597
if I was born to die what the heck

134
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:10,697
was the point of me even Being born I
never made anything or gave anything

135
00:11:10,780 --> 00:11:16,657
to anyone all I did was waste drugs
and hog that Machine and cause

136
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:22,920
trouble for everyone if all I get to
do is suffer and disappear in the end

137
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:26,697
It'd be better to just disappear right

138
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:32,500
now I used to always think why am I alive

139
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:39,317
Why do I stick around for
this long but you know

140
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:44,660
what after all this time
I think I know why now

141
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:51,237
I might not have done much But
I'm glad I got to live Cause

142
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:56,120
after everything These last few
moments They're the best ever

143
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:03,857
I'm surrounded by all
my friends And I got to

144
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:08,420
end my journey In the
arms of someone I love

145
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:16,557
Yuki I promise I will
see you again someday

146
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:21,217
in some other place
some other world I don't

147
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:25,137
know How but I'll find
you and then we can sit

148
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:28,060
and talk and you can
tell me where you've been

149
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,700
I gave this life.

150
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:50,397
Everything I had.

151
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:52,100
I was alive.

152
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:23,860
¶¶

153
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:43,440
I never made anything, or
gave anything to anyone.

154
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:45,940
You gave me something.

155
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:50,920
You carved it deep into my
heart, and it'll always be there.

156
00:13:58,900 --> 00:13:59,900
Hello, Asuna.

157
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:01,060
How are you?

158
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:06,260
Wait, is that you, Siyone?

159
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:08,940
Yes, in the flesh.

160
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:11,517
It's nice to finally meet
you in the real world.

161
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,860
I'm Sheen Ahn.

162
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:14,960
Oh, it's nice to see you, too.

163
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:16,420
I'm Asuna Yuki.

164
00:14:17,660 --> 00:14:19,836
Like meeting for the first time, huh?

165
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:24,997
But no, it's okay.

166
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:27,257
Just this month I got
the all clear from my

167
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:29,477
doctor and was discharged
from the hospital.

168
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:31,480
Then you're doing better?

169
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:32,710
Yes

170
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:37,237
The type of disease I have is
called acute lymphocytic leukemia.

171
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:40,480
And it was about three years
ago when I developed it.

172
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:43,997
The side effects from the
medicine were so horrible!

173
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:46,257
I wanted to die rather
than keep suffering.

174
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:48,960
But whenever I saw Yuki, I thought,

175
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:54,026
here's this kid, and she's handling her
situation better than I'm handling mine.

176
00:14:54,580 --> 00:14:58,345
Around February, they started
cutting back on the meds I was on.

177
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:02,400
I thought, this is it, and
I braced myself for the end.

178
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:09,420
And then a week ago, the day after
Yuki died, my doctor came in and said,

179
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:12,397
congratulations, you're
in complete remission.

180
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:14,657
Next thing I knew, I was being discharged.

181
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:17,740
I barely had a chance to process the news.

182
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:22,380
And the truth is, it
still hasn't sunk in yet.

183
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:25,840
It's like, I should feel awful.

184
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:29,709
It doesn't seem fair that I'm
still here and Yuki's waiting.

185
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:35,660
Yuki and Ron, Clovis and Merida, we
promised we'd stick together forever.

186
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:38,540
And I'm here.

187
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:40,490
Sheen.

188
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:41,950
You know,

189
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:43,557
our lives are like vessels,

190
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:47,228
and we carry the teachings of
the ones who've passed in them.

191
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:50,500
For the longest time, I was so scared.

192
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:53,437
Scared of telling someone
how I really felt,

193
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:55,873
and scared of finding out how they felt.

194
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:59,849
But I learned from Yuki that
that was no way for me to live.

195
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:03,960
If I didn't even try to reach
out, nothing would ever change.

196
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:09,339
She taught me how to be strong, and
I want to share that with others.

197
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:14,680
As long as I'm alive, I'll pass on what
I learned from her to everyone I meet.

198
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:16,260
And then someday,

199
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:20,937
when I see her again, I want to tell
her about all the people she's helped.

200
00:16:21,020 --> 00:16:22,726
That's how I'll pay her back.

201
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:25,380
Thank you, Asuna.

202
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:35,440
You know, we're all so
grateful for what you've done.

203
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,940
I'd been so worried about Yuki.

204
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:43,462
She was carrying a heavy burden
on those little shoulders of hers.

205
00:16:44,260 --> 00:16:47,640
But then you showed up, and
something in her changed.

206
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:52,517
When you were together, Yuki seemed
like she was really having fun.

207
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:56,337
She was like a forgetful bird
who remembered how to fly.

208
00:16:56,420 --> 00:17:01,380
Then she flew up and up, and
now she's out of our reach.

209
00:17:06,460 --> 00:17:08,217
Anyway, June's also doing great.

210
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:10,829
The medication he's on
seems to be working.

211
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:12,700
It's like, I don't know,

212
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:17,057
to me it feels like Yuki's telling all
of us it's still too soon to join her.

213
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:19,637
I guess that means it's
going to be a while yet

214
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:21,797
before the sleeping
knights get back together.

215
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:22,710
Just remember,

216
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:27,665
next time you're taking me in as a member
and I don't want to hear any arguments.

217
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:31,650
Hey.

218
00:17:31,733 --> 00:17:33,660
I hope we're not interrupting anything.

219
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:35,070
No.

220
00:17:35,153 --> 00:17:38,600
But wait, do you guys
know each other? Sort of.

221
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:42,757
He's trying to steal my ideas about
that communications pod I made.

222
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:43,860
No, he's lying.

223
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:47,257
I'm interested in its possibilities
in full-dive medical tech,

224
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:49,575
so we've been emailing back and forth.

225
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:51,497
That's great for both of you.

226
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:53,109
What about the medicuboid?

227
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:56,257
Are you going to phase it out,
or were the trials successful?

228
00:17:56,340 --> 00:17:57,280
Glad you asked.

229
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:59,057
They were extremely successful,

230
00:17:59,140 --> 00:18:02,137
and now we have enough data
to proceed to the next phase.

231
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:04,317
Soon patients all over
the country will have...

232
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:06,340
I am so sorry about that.

233
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:09,000
I can't believe I didn't say this first.

234
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:12,100
Mizan, congratulations on your recovery.

235
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:15,266
I know Yuki would be
thrilled at the news too.

236
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,680
Thank you for saying so.

237
00:18:17,940 --> 00:18:20,040
And congratulations on the trials.

238
00:18:20,420 --> 00:18:24,317
It's good to know what you learned
from Yuki will be used to help others.

239
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,760
That makes me happy. Me too.

240
00:18:27,260 --> 00:18:29,877
Yuki was the first person
to test the medicuboid,

241
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:32,500
and her name will always be remembered.

242
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:35,777
If she were here, she'd
get an award for her help,

243
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:38,860
along with the benefactor
who made it all possible.

244
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:42,866
Knowing Yuki, she wouldn't be
too thrilled at getting an award.

245
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:46,451
She'd say, what's the point in
having it if I can't eat it?

246
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:54,560
Um, Doctor, you just mentioned the
Medicuboid had some kind of benefactor.

247
00:18:54,820 --> 00:18:57,677
I thought you said the
government was paying for it.

248
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,780
Oh, well, yes, they are.

249
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:03,937
But the initial designs were given
to us for free from someone else.

250
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:07,740
If I remember correctly,
I think her name was Dr.

251
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:09,080
Rank Kojiro.

252
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,300
What's wrong, Kirito?

253
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:17,420
I know her.

254
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:18,830
How?

255
00:19:18,913 --> 00:19:19,900
I met her once.

256
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:25,251
Yeah, in fact, she was taking care of
Heathcliff's body while he was diving.

257
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:27,117
She was his head researcher.

258
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,788
She helped him develop
full dive technology.

259
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,280
You see?

260
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:33,240
The Medicuboid's design.

261
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:34,971
You know who invented it?

262
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:36,060
No way.

263
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:38,000
It was Kayaba.

264
00:20:03,020 --> 00:20:06,737
I want to show you what

265
00:20:06,820 --> 00:20:13,377
I want

266
00:20:13,460 --> 00:20:18,977
to

267
00:20:19,060 --> 00:20:21,537
show you.

268
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:25,117
I will always be able to make sure.

269
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:32,060
I don't know when I'm wrong.

270
00:20:32,620 --> 00:20:36,797
I will be able to see you. I will be able

271
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:39,297
to see

272
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:44,677
you?

273
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:50,920
That's what I see when I'm in my eyes.

274
00:20:56,760 --> 00:21:03,060
I want to hear the sound of my voice.

275
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:10,377
I want to hear the

276
00:21:10,460 --> 00:21:14,240
sound of my voice.

277
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:33,617
Need any help unpacking all this stuff?

278
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:35,700
Sure, but only if you're not busy.

279
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:37,680
Seriously, ain't she cute?

280
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:39,920
I got you a little gift.

281
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:41,920
No way, you shouldn't have.

282
00:21:42,060 --> 00:21:43,197
You guys suck.

283
00:21:43,280 --> 00:21:45,897
Are you having fun hanging
out here with everyone?

284
00:21:45,980 --> 00:21:48,333
Yes, and the cherry blossoms are pretty.

285
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:50,737
Yeah, it's too bad they're almost gone.

286
00:21:50,820 --> 00:21:53,644
Oh, please, there's plenty
left, you spoilsport.

287
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:55,407
Anyway, we're here with Yui.

288
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:56,977
That's the important thing.

289
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:59,737
I still can't believe we
made it happen that fast.

290
00:21:59,820 --> 00:22:01,617
Thank you so much for this, Daddy.

291
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:03,160
Yeah, Kirito, thank you.

292
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:07,935
Nah, if you want to thank someone,
thank Yuki for helping me develop it.

293
00:22:12,140 --> 00:22:12,970
Wow!

294
00:22:15,620 --> 00:22:17,580
The real world and the virtual.

295
00:22:18,140 --> 00:22:22,375
I thought the closer they came together,
the better the future would be.

296
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:26,494
It's like, the more the lines
between these worlds blur,

297
00:22:26,860 --> 00:22:29,684
the more everyone gets
sucked into its darkness.

298
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:33,480
Yeah, but a lot of people
have been helped by it, too.

299
00:22:34,760 --> 00:22:38,340
If anything, I wish I knew
what Kayaba's master plan was.

300
00:22:39,040 --> 00:22:40,000
I don't know.

301
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:43,460
Maybe it's our job as
survivors of SAO to find out.

302
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:45,860
I think you're overthinking things.

303
00:22:46,260 --> 00:22:47,180
Yeah, I guess.

304
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:50,340
Still, I want to find
out more than ever now.

305
00:22:50,780 --> 00:22:54,780
Even after everything that's happened,
my curiosity's got me hooked.

306
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:57,797
Although, a part of me
thinks I'm being played here.

307
00:22:57,880 --> 00:22:59,292
That's kind of annoying.

308
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:01,250
Whatever.

309
00:23:01,780 --> 00:23:04,427
I don't know what's
going to happen tomorrow.

310
00:23:04,540 --> 00:23:08,360
All I know is, I want
to be with you forever.

311
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:10,446
And I want you to be with me.

312
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:14,477
I'll stick by you even if you
move halfway across the planet.

313
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:16,400
Who said anything about moving?

314
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:18,760
Don't forget to take Mila.

315
00:23:20,260 --> 00:23:21,460
Hey, lovebirds!

316
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:23,120
Quit making out!

317
00:23:23,220 --> 00:23:24,632
We want to take a photo!

318
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:26,400
Get over here, guys!

319
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:28,220
Come on!

320
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,240
Well, shall we?

321
00:23:30,980 --> 00:23:32,020
Okay, Daddy.

322
00:23:36,220 --> 00:23:37,050
Thank you.
